Report a result so its uncertainty survives later use (@met-reporting: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metrology, #source "../sources/GUM-and-Amendment.lingua#r_3KA76CK3QAA3M470TC3XHP19MQ", #source "../sources/Uncertainty-NIST-1900.lingua#r_75WCVW8CJG4TAFD3330T87588E", #source "../sources/GUM-Multivariate.lingua#r_1S5554FGCGA5E8GKAM6C9KMJKK", #metrology "../applications/Measurement-families.lingua#r_08ZQTJTT3X336JMZC2QKWZZRRF") { r_1DX8JW7A1K3R87MJ4W9AYVJ52D
**Read:** [GUM — JCGM 100:2008 and the 2026 nonlinearity amendment](../sources/GUM-and-Amendment.lingua#r_3KA76CK3QAA3M470TC3XHP19MQ), the reporting clause and relevant uncertainty interpretation; [Simple Guide for Evaluating and Expressing Uncertainty — Possolo](../sources/Uncertainty-NIST-1900.lingua#r_75WCVW8CJG4TAFD3330T87588E), section 8; [Several output quantities — JCGM 102](../sources/GUM-Multivariate.lingua#r_1S5554FGCGA5E8GKAM6C9KMJKK), the treatment of vector results and coverage regions.

A usable result identifies measurand, estimate, unit and reference conditions, uncertainty interpretation, model or method, and relevant source and validity information. Add the coverage factor or interval construction and probability when justified. For vector results preserve dependence. Link the supporting observations and calculation so another person can reconstruct what the compact result means.

For the teaching additive example, x = 20.004 mm with u_c about 0.00539 mm can be reported with expanded uncertainty about 0.011 mm at k = 2 after sensible rounding. The probability interpretation still depends on the assumptions; do not attach an automatic 95% claim. Preserve the underlying unrounded values and evaluation details.

Distinguish the measured estimate from a specification, target value, conformity decision, and prediction of future behavior. If a result is later used at different temperature, range, loading, time, or sample basis, the new use may require additional corrections and uncertainty. A certificate’s concise numerical line does not make those conditions disappear.

**Work:** issue two versions of a teaching report: a compact result for a receiver and a full supporting report. Ask a second reader to use it in a derived quantity and identify any information they lack. Then change the intended use and explain exactly which terms can be reused and which need reassessment.

Record source editions and model revisions, especially when using amended guidance or new reference values. A later correction should say which previous conclusion changes and why. Reliable knowledge transfer requires retaining meaning and limitations through the chain, not only copying the final number into another database.

